  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan ACJR 2024 (Parent)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY
In response to extreme food shortages and catastrophic hunger conditions in Sudan, this Joint Response focuses on two sectors: Food Security and Livelihoods (FSL), and Nutrition. The JR aims to contribute to available of, access to and consumption of food in Darfur. The FSL activities include vouchers, cash assistance, and in-kind support. Besides, lifesaving nutrition interventions will be provided, prioritizing vulnerable children at high mortality risk, and pregnant and lactating women. The partners include1) FPDO (Plan International), 2) Child Development Foundation (Save the Children), 3) SUDO (CARE), 4) World Relief and 5) HOPE (Tearfund), 6) Alsawaid Alkhadara Organization (World Vision), 7) SOS Sahel and 8) GFO (ZOA).

The Joint Response runs from 7 July 2024 until 31 December 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
